---
import StopwatchLayout from '../../layouts/StopwatchLayout.astro';
---

<StopwatchLayout
	title="Online Stopwatch — Free Full-Screen Stopwatch & Lap Timer"
	description="A free, full-screen online stopwatch for tracking laps, split times, and sports or study timing. Works directly in your browser with private local storage."
	schemaName="Online Stopwatch"
	schemaAltName="OS Stopwatch"
>
	<!-- Below the Fold SEO Guide & FAQ Section -->
	<section class="w-full max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-16 group-data-[size=full]/body:hidden">
		<div class="bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900 border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-10 shadow-sm space-y-10">

			<!-- Main Overview -->
			<div>
				<h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-zinc-950 dark:text-zinc-50 tracking-tight mb-4">
					Free Full-Screen Online Stopwatch with Lap & Split Timing
				</h2>
				<div class="text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-base">
					<p>
						Welcome to <strong>On Screen Timer's Online Stopwatch</strong>, a lightweight, precision timing utility engineered for zero-latency measurement directly inside your web browser. Whether you are tracking interval splits during a high-intensity workout, timing classroom exams, pacing presentation slides, or benchmarking operational workflows, our digital stopwatch gives you instant, crystal-clear readability from anywhere in the room.
					</p>
					<p>
						Built without annoying downloads, mobile app installs, or user account signups, our stopwatch loads instantly on any desktop, tablet, or smartphone. The scalable full-screen interface ensures high-contrast visibility under gym lighting, lecture hall projection, or personal workstation standby.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Core Capabilities Grid -->
			<div>
				<h3 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 mb-4">
					Engineered for Absolute Precision & Versatility
				</h3>
				<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
					<div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-zinc-200/80 dark:border-zinc-800/80 bg-zinc-50/50 dark:bg-zinc-950/40">
						<h4 class="font-medium text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm mb-1.5">Millisecond Precision & Split Laps</h4>
						<p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
							Count upward with hundredths-of-a-second accuracy. Hit the Lap button anytime to record instant segment splits alongside your cumulative elapsed time in a clean, scrollable log table.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-zinc-200/80 dark:border-zinc-800/80 bg-zinc-50/50 dark:bg-zinc-950/40">
						<h4 class="font-medium text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm mb-1.5">Full-Screen & High-Contrast Display</h4>
						<p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
							Scale the display up to maximum monitor dimensions. Switch effortlessly between Modern, Digital SVG font, and Classic Analog dials with full dark mode support.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-zinc-200/80 dark:border-zinc-800/80 bg-zinc-50/50 dark:bg-zinc-950/40">
						<h4 class="font-medium text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm mb-1.5">Rapid Keyboard Shortcuts</h4>
						<p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
							Keep your hands on the keyboard. Tap <kbd class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-zinc-200 dark:bg-zinc-800 text-xs font-mono">Space</kbd> to Start or Pause, <kbd class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-zinc-200 dark:bg-zinc-800 text-xs font-mono">R</kbd> to Reset, and <kbd class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-zinc-200 dark:bg-zinc-800 text-xs font-mono">F</kbd> for immersive Full Screen.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-zinc-200/80 dark:border-zinc-800/80 bg-zinc-50/50 dark:bg-zinc-950/40">
						<h4 class="font-medium text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm mb-1.5">Private by Design Local Storage</h4>
						<p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
							All recorded laps, timer preferences, and active tasks remain isolated in your browser’s local storage. Zero data leaves your device, and sessions resume automatically if the page refreshes.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Everyday Applications -->
			<div>
				<h3 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 mb-3">
					Ideal Everyday Use Cases
				</h3>
				<ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2.5 text-sm sm:text-base text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
					<li><strong class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-200">Athletics & Fitness Training:</strong> Accurately time track sprints, swimming laps, circuit intervals, and rest periods between heavy gym sets.</li>
					<li><strong class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-200">Study Sessions & Standardized Tests:</strong> Benchmark reading speed, practice exam section timing, and keep accurate logs of focused study stamina.</li>
					<li><strong class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-200">Speech & Presentation Rehearsal:</strong> Ensure keynote addresses, conference pitches, and webinar segments align strictly with designated schedule limits.</li>
					<li><strong class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-200">Laboratory & Culinary Timing:</strong> Monitor exact chemical reaction intervals, fermentation durations, and coffee brew extractions with decimal precision.</li>
				</ul>
			</div>

			<!-- FAQ Section -->
			<div class="pt-6 border-t border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800">
				<h3 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 mb-6">
					Frequently Asked Questions
				</h3>
				<div class="space-y-4">
					<details class="group border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 rounded-xl bg-zinc-50/50 dark:bg-zinc-950/30">
						<summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer p-4 font-medium text-sm text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-blue-500 rounded-xl">
							How accurate is this online stopwatch?
							<svg class="w-4 h-4 text-zinc-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform shrink-0 ml-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg>
						</summary>
						<div class="p-4 pt-0 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
							Our stopwatch relies on the browser's high-resolution Performance API timestamp calculations rather than simple periodic timeouts. This ensures millisecond-level precision without temporal drift, even when other browser tabs or background processes are running.
						</div>
					</details>

					<details class="group border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 rounded-xl bg-zinc-50/50 dark:bg-zinc-950/30">
						<summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer p-4 font-medium text-sm text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-blue-500 rounded-xl">
							Do my recorded laps stay saved if I reload the browser?
							<svg class="w-4 h-4 text-zinc-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform shrink-0 ml-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg>
						</summary>
						<div class="p-4 pt-0 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
							Yes! Every lap split and overall elapsed timing value is persisted in your browser's private <code class="text-xs bg-zinc-200 dark:bg-zinc-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">localStorage</code>. If your tab reloads or the browser restarts, your session and laps will instantly restore.
						</div>
					</details>

					<details class="group border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 rounded-xl bg-zinc-50/50 dark:bg-zinc-950/30">
						<summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer p-4 font-medium text-sm text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-blue-500 rounded-xl">
							How do I trigger full-screen mode on a projector or TV?
							<svg class="w-4 h-4 text-zinc-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform shrink-0 ml-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg>
						</summary>
						<div class="p-4 pt-0 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
							Simply press the <kbd class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-zinc-200 dark:bg-zinc-800 text-xs font-mono">F</kbd> key on your keyboard or select "Full" from the Size dropdown menu. All peripheral UI elements and headers will collapse, expanding the digits to maximize screen real estate.
						</div>
					</details>

					<details class="group border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 rounded-xl bg-zinc-50/50 dark:bg-zinc-950/30">
						<summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer p-4 font-medium text-sm text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-blue-500 rounded-xl">
							Is any of my timing or activity data sent to third-party servers?
							<svg class="w-4 h-4 text-zinc-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform shrink-0 ml-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg>
						</summary>
						<div class="p-4 pt-0 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
							No. Under our "Private by Design" policy, 100% of stopwatch calculation, lap logging, and task management happens client-side in your device's browser engine. No user timing records are ever stored on cloud servers.
						</div>
					</details>
				</div>
			</div>

		</div>
	</section>
</StopwatchLayout>
